{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"5597dfa12f907d67","type":"text","text":"==Cursed Items==","x":-145,"y":-20,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"3dd22035362c5204","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Due to the increase in sin activities, TEMERITY has allowed the opening of the Cursed Item arsenal to all CAT 2+ exorcists. They may be purchased as specialized weapons with specific bonuses and count as your service weapon. Flavour is free as always.","x":260,"y":-90,"width":459,"height":200},
		{"id":"afef7acfa04a3600","type":"text","text":"==Using cursed items==","x":848,"y":-20,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"6aab5543aec0475c","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> (Addendum: This time of relic ==can be== acquired from Chapter 1 instead of the more pure and unique ones, you can also \"sacrifice\" it to form your Coded weapon without sacrificing sin!)","x":321,"y":-400,"width":338,"height":220},
		{"id":"ffff0b43b474a83f","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Cursed Items are specialized items created from the remains of executed sins gathered over the course of your journey under CAIN. Starting with ==CAT 2==, your exorcist is eligible to purchase their very own cursed item at the cost of ==5 scrip==. Your cursed item ==scales with your service weapon’s CAT level==, counts as a ==service weapon==, and ==is pulled out for 3 KP==.","x":1260,"y":-120,"width":420,"height":260},
		{"id":"9e047b68d83a1407","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> (Addendum: for the campaign itself, consider this type of item to fall into the terms \"Common degree Relics\" and \"Relics\" for future rules and descriptions)","x":-201,"y":-340,"width":362,"height":200},
		{"id":"611bec3fdd7a7077","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> The Administration: About the mass production of Relics Replica and its acquisition by operatives.\n> \n> Although authorized Warehouse copies and modification are allowed under the gaze of The Administration, be aware that such objects are bound to one day be prohibited under following UN proposal in the future.\n> \n> Do not become dependant of cheap copies, its cost of production in human lives is not worth to keep in the future going forward, we are more civilized that those black markets profiting of human suffering.\n\n","x":1210,"y":-600,"width":520,"height":350},
		{"id":"3e74444aa5853f46","type":"text","text":"==Customization & Purchase==","x":1345,"y":300,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"0b353228f07c1c84","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Upon purchasing a cursed item, you decide of its ==appearance==, its ==curse==, and one of the available ==effects== listed on the weapon. Each sin type have guidelines to help your creativity but you can also choose a custom appearances and curse with your Admin. Your cursed item is not required to be shaped like an actual weapon, it can be clothes, accessories, or other…","x":753,"y":195,"width":440,"height":270},
		{"id":"ec4d0846f12818f9","type":"text","text":"==Upgrades==","x":365,"y":300,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"ccfecd25ea3ed772","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> You ==upgrade== your cursed item automatically by upgrading your service weapon’s CAT, gaining ==an additional curse== and ==an additional effect==. Your cursed item can only hold up to ==your service weapon’s CAT+1== amount of effects at once. If you have no more room for an effect, you may replace a previous effect with a new one either during the upgrade process, or by spending 2 scrip between missions.","x":-250,"y":195,"width":460,"height":271},
		{"id":"159ccf4b9506745c","type":"text","text":"==Curses & effects==","x":-720,"y":301,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"165c6fc5ad6c6ed8","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Effects are special benefits and the raison d’être of your cursed item’s existence. When you first purchase a cursed item, you grant it ==one available unique effect== depending on the sin type it originates from. Later, you can upgrade it as you ==upgrade== your service weapon, or by paying ==2 scrip to replace== a previous one, granting it an additional effect from any sin type at the cost of an additional curse from the same type as the effect gained. By replacing an effect, you also replace its associated curse. If you buy a cursed item ==after== you’ve upgraded your service weapons, it ==upgrades automatically== to the correct scale and you may pick additional curses and effects accordingly.","x":-813,"y":466,"width":438,"height":434},
		{"id":"c68e1a4bb2fad8a2","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> During the hunt, the Admin may call upon the curse of your weapon to make a ==Threat (1-3)== or a ==Complication (1-3)== which you must deal with before you can continue using the item normally. That threat deals 2 stress by default, with each curses granting +1 stress to its threat or granting +1 slash to its related complication talisman (min. 2 slashes).","x":-778,"y":-120,"width":367,"height":321},
		{"id":"88422119ef206302","type":"text","text":"==Loss of Cain property== ","x":-1360,"y":301,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"b358e779ccb46e11","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> If you lose a cursed item, you are docked ==your service weapon’s CAT+2 scrip== at the end of the hunt to replace it. This is considered a huge dishonor and may cause disciplinary actions against you by TEMERITY agents.","x":-1880,"y":221,"width":380,"height":219},
		{"id":"7c6ddb95a1f10b9b","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> (Addendum: The only exception is the \"sacrificing the relic\" to manifest the coded one, which will only cost you in penalization ==2 scrip== instead)","x":-1846,"y":-120,"width":313,"height":203},
		{"id":"2650fd1e9f393615","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Your Admin may restrict cursed item’s effects according to your personal hunt history, making you unable to gain effects made from sins you haven’t executed yet, or even can create custom effects specific to sins you slew.","x":-2460,"y":229,"width":440,"height":204},
		{"id":"848a606f14100f72","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> (Addendum: :3)","x":-2382,"y":560,"width":284,"height":87},
		{"id":"b498d35b2ade816f","type":"text","text":"==Perfect Sins==","x":-620,"y":-700,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"ecb550e9ec754fa8","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Perfect sins are special grade targets feared by both senior exorcists and CAIN staff. While extremely rare, their presence can radically shift the psychic sea causing any manifestation to be swiftly targeted for total obliteration of its existence.","x":-1100,"y":-790,"width":367,"height":240},
		{"id":"c97bc6c77c4d083e","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> With the growing pressures of reality, SEER has been able to research more on these entities and their potent strength allowing for earlier detection and destruction of their hosts pre-manifestation. This, however, seem to have echoed within the psychic sea causing a surge reaction back into each perfect sin granting them ==additional complications== and ==perfect abilities== detailed here. These may be added to any perfect sin in your games for additional variety and difficulty.","x":-1134,"y":-1260,"width":436,"height":340},
		{"id":"bf205714154c19b4","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Options are present between pages 13-19 in case you want to check for yourself!","x":-1080,"y":257,"width":315,"height":148},
		{"id":"ee7fe90d8ca227f0","type":"text","text":"==Improved abilities==","x":-540,"y":-1115,"width":233,"height":50},
		{"id":"98a4be011f8077c8","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Each may be taken by any perfect sins instead of one of their usual perfect abilities, replacing them.","x":-160,"y":-1160,"width":356,"height":141},
		{"id":"f05a24a74f582c53","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> ==◊ Perfect Pressure==: Pressure is slashed two times when tension fills up or when resting. A conflict scene may tick up tension once per pressure after its resolved.","x":-642,"y":-920,"width":482,"height":156},
		{"id":"568f690fd5db5bcd","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> ==◊ Perfect Minion==: The Perfect Sin’s traces gain either +2 slashes to their execution talisman OR deal +1 stress with their reaction. Chosen upon taking this ability","x":141,"y":-915,"width":419,"height":175},
		{"id":"ed6038e68bb40ac9","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> ==◊ Worldsplinter Edge==: The Perfect Sin’s attacks may reach beyond the horizon to, once per scene, roll a reaction against the exorcists from a different area or scene.","x":141,"y":-1448,"width":365,"height":188},
		{"id":"5f2dd213d2c9b6e0","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> ==◊ Absolute Obliteration==: The Perfect Sin may use its Severe Attack on a 1-3 reaction instead of only on a 1 reaction. However, it deals -1 stress to all affected exorcists.","x":-423,"y":-1448,"width":384,"height":188},
		{"id":"b277f8c903b322c9","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> ==EK flight module==: Action shorter than long range become impossible against the sin.\n> \n> ","x":368,"y":-1154,"width":385,"height":130},
		{"id":"6d899557f148f165","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> ==Ominous==: Once per round, may make a threat in addition to a 1-3 reaction that doesn’t count to the threat per round limit.","x":920,"y":-1177,"width":350,"height":176},
		{"id":"a1209c6eca8f8895","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> ==EK tension edge:== +1 stress dealt against exorcists above half their injury cap.","x":1500,"y":-1160,"width":348,"height":143},
		{"id":"e3fc5ae6be63cac2","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> ==Heartache==: Exorcists are unable to start teamwork or setup with eachother.","x":1270,"y":-880,"width":330,"height":140},
		{"id":"34bb380528775f11","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> ==Laceration==: On any 6 reaction, deal 1 stress to all exorcists in the scene.","x":753,"y":-880,"width":325,"height":134},
		{"id":"628a4fb43d8048fe","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Imperfect sins variants are present from page 67 to 69!","x":-1070,"y":-1503,"width":308,"height":111},
		{"id":"827aeb7968a9a13a","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> The Administration: About the possible existence of Stage 4 worms.\n> \n> Do not question this line of thought further beyond this point.\n> \n> This is our final warning.","x":-1660,"y":-956,"width":420,"height":229},
		{"id":"3119acb35e2c6d10","type":"text","text":"==GREATER SIN==","x":-1575,"y":-1260,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"7bfc0aceb3c9277d","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Time is a cycle, continuing and intensifying in a loop of psychic energy surrounding every human’s needs and emotions. Sins are manifested from the single trauma of man birthed to protect them from the outside world. Yet no matter their attempt, that shield cannot fully protect them from harm.","x":-2100,"y":-1349,"width":420,"height":238},
		{"id":"11a65669d4e1a71d","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Faced with this eternal problem, sins in recent history have mutated becoming stronger and more durable to face reality. These mutations are attributed the title of ==🟣GREATER SIN==.","x":-2078,"y":-1698,"width":377,"height":251},
		{"id":"437b3e246c50c065","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> In the following section, you will find rules to strengthen and modify your sins to make them more threatening to your players or make your hunts more impactful and tense. These special mutations are excellent tools for making impactful one-shots to your players.","x":-2640,"y":-1711,"width":360,"height":278},
		{"id":"9a2d499d85dc7b32","type":"text","text":"==How to use==","x":-2585,"y":-1920,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"d506769212246b67","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> With the increase in potency from sins and exorcists alike, you may want to spice up your missions with intensifying circumstances without feeling the need to pull out your perfect sin card. It is at that moment that a greater sin’s hunt is best suited for!","x":-2633,"y":-2280,"width":346,"height":260},
		{"id":"9649dd38047ce1ff","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Greater sins are akin to mini-bosses in your campaign, filling the need for a powerful and impactful hunt without needing to bring the big guns yet. On this page and the next you’ll find modifiers that change the hunt and the sin’s impact on the game. These mutations may be combined together or played one at a time, it is best advised to tell the players ahead of time that they will face such a sin and what kind of mutation they have.","x":-2100,"y":-2281,"width":509,"height":261},
		{"id":"9e147803aae1ab79","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> When making your selection of mutations, you may pick any of them up to a number of times equal to half the sin’s CAT rounded up. This is a maximum, and you may decide to have less mutation selected than the sin could have.","x":-1380,"y":-2249,"width":424,"height":199},
		{"id":"ddfcd80ba40953cf","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> You may also cause the sin to gain a mutation while in the middle of a hunt, this is treated as making a ==threat== or ==tension move==.","x":-1344,"y":-2560,"width":352,"height":178},
		{"id":"a8b1ea1c846a48ce","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> The Administration: About Plague type execution operations and the possibility of Stage 4 forming naturally.\n> \n> ~~We are even allowed to talk about this? I already got called for a security meeting with Him just because I was thinking about this shit!~~","x":-1520,"y":-1698,"width":390,"height":257},
		{"id":"ad4bd464eb53ab72","type":"text","text":"==GREATER PERFECT SN==","x":-1293,"y":-2780,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"5051fb492a597238","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Greater sins are a seperate modifier to being a perfect sin, would you be able to fuse both into one greater perfect sin? Yes actually. \n> \n> When making a perfect sin into a greater sin, you may have them mutate up to CAT times per hunt instead of only ½ CAT.","x":-820,"y":-2869,"width":414,"height":238},
		{"id":"a3530fb53245d1f1","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> However, be careful in moderation as a greater perfect sin may create situations that are impossible or outright lethal to an unprepared team, and is best suited for the end of a long lasting campaign with players aware of what they are facing.","x":-180,"y":-2859,"width":420,"height":218},
		{"id":"8d3a6789c2791d6f","type":"text","text":"*SHE*","x":-91,"y":-2569,"width":51,"height":89,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"0752bc431eb4e5a0","type":"text","text":"*AWAITS*","x":-225,"y":-2412,"width":50,"height":161,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"1434d2a44ec49f11","type":"text","text":"*IN*","x":-96,"y":-2220,"width":56,"height":60,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"0bfcb2bb7d567ea9","type":"text","text":"*SOUND*","x":-96,"y":-1900,"width":51,"height":140,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"7abd68f61626cce8","type":"text","text":"*THE*","x":-205,"y":-2080,"width":60,"height":90,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"26400e9bf18bea36","type":"text","text":" ==IMAGO GREATER SIN==","x":440,"y":-2780,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"8a490127342be1dc","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> As an exorcists, CAIN expects your inevitable end to come in various ways. With the increase in perfect sin activity, it was found that Imago created by exorcists generally became perfect sins if allowed to flee. However, with the new found research on Greater Sins, a new unfortunate situation has arrived.","x":880,"y":-2877,"width":440,"height":254},
		{"id":"79d6700abb93d52a","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Exorcists who imago due to giving up on their resistance roll, may make their Imago become a Greater Sin right away, instead of a normal Imago. These Greater Imago may gain a number of mutations equal to ½ CAT of their exorcist’s counterpart.","x":927,"y":-2500,"width":346,"height":245},
		{"id":"4724d0c346c1e877","type":"text","text":"==Greater reward==","x":1460,"y":-2407,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"87c3fb1b49915a5b","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Fighting a greater sin can be a crueling task, especially if they are an imago or a perfect sin. As such, exorcists who manage to execute a greater sin are rewarded an additional +3 scrip, and an additional +3 scrip if they are a greater perfect sin.","x":1397,"y":-2820,"width":376,"height":263},
		{"id":"8cc44af906ea5f3f","type":"text","text":"==Sin upgrades==","x":1460,"y":-3120,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"4822048cbb9fe890","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> If you believe your sin is too weak during a conflict scene, or your exorcists are too powerful, you may utilize the following reaction tables instead of the usual ones: \n> \n> - ==Deal devastating stress==: ==(1)== 6 stress, ==(2-3)== 4 stress, ==(4+)== 3 stress. \n>   \n> - ==Deal sinful stress:== ==(1==) 5 stress + 2 sin, ==(2-3)== 3 stress + 1 sin, ==(4+)== 2 stress. \n>   \n> - ==Deal mental stress: (1)== 5 stress + an affliction, ==(2-3)== 3 stress + an affliction, ==(4+)== 2 stress. \n>   \n>   You may only pick ==one table per sin== when you first create them","x":812,"y":-3280,"width":508,"height":380},
		{"id":"e37ae3c36e3eed93","type":"text","text":"==Mutation==","x":260,"y":-3121,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"78a21023562f0f63","type":"text","text":"==Greater sin list==","x":-219,"y":-3123,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"7bb7ebc8c9e9a14a","x":-290,"y":-3480,"width":392,"height":260,"type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> ==Wretched soul==\n> \n> The Greater Sin is able to create intense hazards in the investigation area. At the start of any scene, you may cause the area to be hazardous. Until the exorcists are able to restore the area, any actions become risky while within it."},
		{"id":"e6a72fd91790e410","x":-840,"y":-3916,"width":385,"height":261,"type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> ==Escalating end==\n> \n> The Greater Sin has such dangerous ideals, their actions within the investigation area intensify their end. The pressure talisman becomes halved (6 to 3), any ability or stats related to pressure count it as double than its current value (rounded up)."},
		{"id":"5c0fe91d16c8ceb9","x":280,"y":-3910,"width":318,"height":250,"type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> ==Crooked luck==\n> \n> The Greater Sin’s depressing humor causes the luck of the investigation area to go down. ==All action rolls can only succeed on a 5+ result,== rather than the typical result of 4+."},
		{"id":"acfa13d8093e2091","x":-816,"y":-4480,"width":338,"height":281,"type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> ==Hellish hide==\n> \n> The Greater Sin’s body is tough to endure the pain of reality. When setting up the hunt’s sin, use the following Execution Talisman: \n> \n> ==7 + PRESSURE + CAT + (Number of XO x 2)=="},
		{"id":"26d329e3388d2f80","x":-300,"y":-4239,"width":389,"height":454,"type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Eve's apple\n> \n> The Greater Sin gained awareness of a grand truth beyond the exorcist’s knowledge. As a ==tension move==, the sin may apply one of the following effects to a player outside the game: - They are unable to talk or hear other players. - Their character becomes aware of the admin and the players’ existence until the scene ends. - The player must scratch out or delete their notes about the host and sin. Their character forgets all those informations as well. - Their character permanently gains the unbolded agenda item: Seek out secrets outside reality."},
		{"id":"9aec829b1b31170e","x":240,"y":-4509,"width":320,"height":340,"type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> ==Boiling hearth==\n> \n> The Greater Sin’s rage alters the very air within the investigation area. Weather is altered to a violent and extreme variable, harsh rain, intense heatwave, sheer cold, etc… Any actions not inside of a building protected from outside is hard by default, even with teamwork or setup."}
	],
	"edges":[
